  "step_3": "The decision reason requires: (1) identifying outcomes with probability > 1/n (n = number of outcomes), and (2) computing the average of those probable outcomes. In this case, only 0 Euros is probable in both lotteries (since 0.75 and 0.50 are > 0.5 and 0.333 respectively, but only 0 is non-zero and thus the only probable outcome), so both have zero average of probable outcomes. The reason would be indifferent. However, the individual’s justification is not about applying this rule. Instead, the individual says 'höhere wahrscheinlichkeit auf gewinn', which implies a focus on the probability of winning something (i.e., avoiding zero), not on classifying outcomes as probable under the 1/n threshold. There is no mention of the threshold, the categorization of outcomes, or the averaging of probable outcomes. Therefore, the individual did not use the specific decision reason as defined. The reasoning is conceptually related (both involve probability of winning), but the mechanism and criteria differ. Thus, the decision reason was not used in the described deliberation process.",
